{
  "family": "corporate",
  "familyName": "Professional",
  "summary": "Clear, dependable and orderly: the look of software people trust with their work.",
  "principles": [
    "Every screen has a clear structure: header, content, actions.",
    "Light borders and soft shadows lift cards a little.",
    "Status is shown with small tinted badges, never colour alone.",
    "Numbers align right; dense where it helps, never cramped."
  ],
  "componentNotes": [
    "Cards: white surface, 1px border, small soft shadow, 8px corners.",
    "Buttons: primary solid, secondary outlined, destructive in the error colour; 8px corners.",
    "Tables: a tinted header row, row hairlines, numbers aligned right.",
    "Navigation: a left sidebar for apps, a top bar with a clear call to action for sites.",
    "Badges: small, tinted background with matching darker text."
  ],
  "personality": "- Components (the kit draws them this way; use the ds-* classes and never restyle them): corners soft, depth subtle, spacing balanced, type balanced; buttons solid, cards bordered, inputs boxed, navigation pill, tables lines, icons regular.\n- Colour amount 2 of 4: colour on actions, highlights and one band a page.\n- Voice: Clear, polite and direct. No jargon, no jokes; every label names its action. Write every label, heading, empty state and message this way.",
